## Implementation progress — 2026-09-23

Implemented on `fix/runtime-artifact-convergence`:

- [x] permanent Standards First rule in Development Guidelines;
- [x] JSON Schema 2020-12 contract layout under `contracts/`;
- [x] provider-neutral service schemas for sql, cache, object-storage, secrets, messaging, vector, observability and identity;
- [x] Service Binding 1.1 aligned binding schema and canonical output-name validation;
- [x] `secure-binding/v1` explicitly reduced to BaseHarbor security/lifecycle extension semantics rather than competing connection-field vocabulary;
- [x] provider descriptor schema with independent provider version and `builtin | oci` distribution;
- [x] Runtime Provider Registry vs Provider Catalog separation documented;
- [x] current v0.4 capability specs classified against the standards-first target model without blind renames;
- [x] ADR 0013 and standards/gap matrix;
- [x] pre-release documentation audit now requires standards review;
- [x] #210/#363/#167/#170/#175/#298/#300/#174 linked to this architecture.

Still to prove before closing #390:
- [ ] exact-head source/spec/docs tests green;
- [ ] compatibility/migration behavior stays intact in executable acceptance;
- [ ] final pre-v0.5 contract review confirms no product-specific service fields leaked into portable intent.

No provider marketplace, dynamic loader or mass capability-ID rename was introduced.
